Pit camera left wrap and signed WORD offsets. Original Pit_Camera_Control
0x429e2c/0x429e35 decrements the signed section and uses JGE: section zero
wraps to five and decrements the revolution count at 0x429e37. The unsigned
reconstruction left section 0xffffffff and indexed before the offset table.
This caused the first late championship picture difference on level seven.
Replay uses the identical signed wrap at 0x429c49/0x429c52.

Both paths test camera_offset as a signed WORD (0x429eb8/0x429ebb and
0x429ccb/0x429cce). Both left-offset loads are WORDs at 0x464a68+section*4
(0x429e24/0x429c41), not DWORD pointer arithmetic at section*8.

--- a/dd2_symbols.h
+++ b/dd2_symbols.h
@@ -939,1 +939,1 @@
-#define camera_offset (*(undefined2*)GIMG(0x00464a88))
+#define camera_offset (*(short*)GIMG(0x00464a88))
@@ -1166,1 +1166,1 @@
-#define camera_section (*(undefined4*)GIMG(0x00464a84))
+#define camera_section (*(int*)GIMG(0x00464a84))
--- a/dd2.c
+++ b/dd2.c
@@ -17973,1 +17973,1 @@
-      camera_offset = (&Old_Cam_Mode)[camera_section * 2];
+      camera_offset = *(short *)((byte *)&Old_Cam_Mode + camera_section * 4);
@@ -18056,1 +18056,1 @@
-      camera_offset = (&Old_Cam_Mode)[camera_section * 2];
+      camera_offset = *(short *)((byte *)&Old_Cam_Mode + camera_section * 4);
